  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Right now the error/warning is something about a failed System.IO.Move statement which confuses users and it also leaves a garbage prefab asset in the project files that may accumulate after each failed compilation. It would be best to completely remove that asset and perhaps enclose that statement under a file check or try block so that if it fails, a meaningful error should be displayed. example: \"Compile errors detected. Avatar building failed. Delete or repair above files to continue.\"\n\nShould be a pretty simple fix. Maybe it might also occur if the file is unabled to be moved because of read/write restrictions, so make sure to check for that as well.",
